Summary: Report network address changes on macOS
Category: system
Kind: fix
Origin: winehq
  Version: 10.8
  Commit: 343954a86d5ab5f7a094a48d9d75128fe734d88d, 84deba0d1a3e5e15ba4803d3001f80900d5d9aa4
  MR: 8048
  Authors: Brendan Shanks
  Changes: as WineHQ's, except that recv()'s result is compared as an int
    (WineHQ's len < sizeof(msg) converts -1 to size_t, so a recv error was
    never seen and a persistent one spun winedevice at full CPU), and EINTR
    is only taken from a failed recv
Origin: crossover
  Version: 25.1.1
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-25.1.1.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/nsiproxy.sys/nsi.c, dlls/nsiproxy.sys/device.c
  Note: taken from CX 25.1.1, which carries the WineHQ change; CX's wow64
    unix-call thunks for nsiproxy are left out (not in 10.0_8). Sikarugir
    10.0_8 ships it: nsiproxy.so: 'PF_SYSTEM socket creation failed',
    'SIOCSKEVFILT failed', 'error receiving, len %d'; nsiproxy.sys:
    UTF-16 wine_nsi_request, wine_nsi_notification; nsiproxy.so has no
    __wine_unix_call_wow64_funcs
Upstream: yes (Wine 10.8); the recv() comparison fix is a candidate (draft
 in .local/bug-reports/)
Needed until: 10.8 (WineHQ has it from 10.8)
Why: On macOS, Wine 10.0's nsiproxy only watched netlink (Linux), so
 NotifyAddrChange and NotifyIpInterfaceChange never fired. Watch a
 PF_SYSTEM kernel event socket for IPv4/IPv6 address events instead, and
 name nsiproxy's threads.
Programs: none known; needed by winhttp-cache-autoproxy to notice network
 changes (Steam)
Messages: "PF_SYSTEM socket creation failed, errno %d.", "SIOCSKEVFILT
 failed, errno %d.", "error receiving, len %d, errno %d." (ERR, channel
 nsi; WINEDEBUG=-all hides them)
No test: needs a network change
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: recv errors seen (signed comparison); not yet in
 a build
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

